{
  "case_id": "2008-07-562",
  "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Altria Group, Inc., et al.",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents' state law claims track nearly verbatim the Cigarette Labeling Act's pre-emption provision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it a question of just how you phrase it, Mr. Olson? Is there any scope -- does your argument leave any scope for attorney general, state attorney general imposition of state law remedies against a deceptive practice involving advertising cigarettes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Olson, doesn't your answer in effect, in practical terms, exclude the possibility of inserts like that? I mean, what else would they be addressing except smoking and health?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But suppose that a new drug is found for the treatment of a condition, glaucoma -- hypothetical -- and the evidence is stunningly clear that smoking with this new drug causes a severe allergic reaction. Does the cigarette manufacturer have any duty to disclose this on the label or in promotions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, in your view, it says in Cipollone that this -- that the four people said in Cipollone that this statute does not pre-empt State law where it's based on a prohibition of making a false statement of material fact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is the argument, and the Respondents are making that argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the prohibition you're talking about is in 13 -- in your express pre-emption argument -- 1334(b). And I was just going to ask you, is a State requirement prohibiting false statements about smoking and health a requirement based on smoking and health?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, Mr. Olson, isn't the problem that Congress was equally clear, or has at least been assumed to be equally clear, in a contrary line of reasoning that holds against you? And that line of reasoning is this: You agree -- everybody agrees -- that the FTC can represent -- it can regulate advertising and -- and supposed deception on matters that do affect -- relate to smoking and health."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, no. As a matter of fact, I could not disagree more, Justice Souter. That's the general background scheme. Then Congress specifically addresses smoking and health in the advertising of cigarettes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States Government",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the United States Government did not address in this case the express pre-emption argument. But a few years ago, in the Reilly case, having to do with the very same statute, the Cigarette Labeling Act, the United States Government said that the labeling act pre-empted State laws concerning the content of cigarette advertising, the content of cigarette advertising."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When Congress enacted the Labeling Act, the 1969 Labeling Act, it gave no intention whatsoever to immunize cigarette makers for the false statements that they made in violation of anti-deception in the marketplace rules."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Frederick, are you saying that the consent decree -- because we have overtaken Judge Kessler's decision by consent decree, right and it has terms? Does a -- does a consent decree terms allow state attorney generals to say don't advertise low?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0001-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ordered here would be superseded by the United States RICO case, where the District Court of the District of Columbia has already issued an injunction for the use of light cigarettes because Judge Kessler found in more than 4,000 findings of fact that Philip Morris had engaged in deception in the marketplace and findings of fact, beginning 2023 and following --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the cigarette companies knew for decades that there was no difference in the yield for low tar and light cigarettes came to light."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could a state attorney general say under my authority to check against false and deceptive advertising, no cigarette company can advertise in this State low or light?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's correct. That was the general purpose of the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2008-07-562",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c46f3eea9ab7f06994bc2fa2fa732a2461cbc470cc53addcb66950aaf0a5c7a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c46f3eea9ab7-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:07 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
